<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19342" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gaurus</span></b> , i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mountain in
			Campania</i>, <i>famous for its wine</i>, now <i>Monte Barbaro</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 6,
				8, § 64</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 1,
				16, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Agr. 2, 14, 36</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gaurus inanis (as producing little),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv. 9,
					57</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gaurā-nus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Mount Gaurus</i>, <i>Gauran</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 9, § 60</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mons,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the Gaurus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 8, 546</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saltus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					2, 6, 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vites,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 3, 4, § 38</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					14, 6, 8, § 63</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ostrea,</span>”
				i. e. <i>from the Lucrine lake</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Juv. 8,
					86</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
